1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,146
BARBARA: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:06,629
Oh, no. Help me! Help
me! Somebody help!

3
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:09,894
COBBLEPOT: <i>They think she
might have fallen asleep at the wheel.</i>

4
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:11,303
ED: <i>Her brake lines were cut.</i>

5
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,314
Which leaves one
conclusion. Murder.

6
00:00:13,647 --> 00:00:15,172
<i>And I know who did it.</i>

7
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:17,007
Hold on, Butch.

8
00:00:18,485 --> 00:00:20,386
IVY: <i>I might be in
trouble. I stole a necklace.</i>

9
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,265
BRUCE: <i>Why is this
necklace so important?</i>

10
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:23,689
<i>What makes someone kill for it?</i>

11
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:25,018
- What is it?
- A key.

12
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:26,558
SELINA: <i>We need to go somewhere.</i>

13
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:27,956
BRUCE: <i>We'll go to my house.</i>

14
00:00:28,161 --> 00:00:29,288
You two are a couple now?

15
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:30,964
- No.
- Yes.

16
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:34,477
My engagement announcement is
coming out in the <i>Gazette</i> tomorrow.

17
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:37,369
And it will feature Mario's
name. His family name.

18
00:00:37,905 --> 00:00:39,373
JIM: <i>You mean Falcone?</i>

19
00:00:41,642 --> 00:00:43,804
Such a beautiful space
for a rehearsal dinner.

20
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:45,570
We can't thank you enough.

21
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:48,439
And did Roberto's food
live up to all my hype?

22
00:00:48,815 --> 00:00:50,113
Are you kidding?

23
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:51,843
(SIGHS) Any more burrata,

24
00:00:52,019 --> 00:00:54,059
and I wouldn't fit into my
wedding dress. (CHUCKLES)

25
00:00:54,788 --> 00:00:56,814
I can't believe we're
getting married in two days.

26
00:00:56,990 --> 00:01:00,085
Have you two settled on
a honeymoon destination?

27
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:03,389
Uh, no, but Lee finally agreed
to take some time off of work.

28
00:01:03,597 --> 00:01:06,328
With everything going on, I didn't
wanna leave anybody in the lurch.

29
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,933
I was very sorry to hear
about Captain Barnes.

30
00:01:09,636 --> 00:01:13,471
He's a good man. What he
did was due entirely to the virus.

31
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:17,372
What's truly frightening is that
nobody knew. Nobody could see it.

32
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:18,876
There aren't any symptoms?

33
00:01:19,346 --> 00:01:23,442
Well, looking back now, there were signs.
Increased strength, emotional instability.

34
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:25,278
Nothing he couldn't hide.

35
00:01:25,552 --> 00:01:27,196
DR. THOMPKINS: <i>The lab
analyzing Alice Tetch's blood</i>

36
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:29,553
has developed a test to
see if someone's infected.

37
00:01:29,823 --> 00:01:32,122
- You're kidding. When?
- They just finished.

38
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:34,193
It's a step toward
finding a cure.

39
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:36,424
How are we? Good?

40
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:39,328
Wonderful, Roberto. We
can't wait for tomorrow night.

41
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,167
Oh! Your rehearsal
dinner's gonna be <i>fantastico.</i>

42
00:01:42,469 --> 00:01:43,937
We're gonna take
care of everything.

43
00:01:44,471 --> 00:01:46,940
It's a privilege to serve
you again, Don Falcone.

44
00:01:57,284 --> 00:02:00,550
Don Falcone, please,
we'll pull your car around.

45
00:02:00,721 --> 00:02:01,721
Yeah, okay.

46
00:02:02,356 --> 00:02:04,848
- Wonderful evening, Roberto.
- You're welcome.

47
00:02:07,394 --> 00:02:10,922
- I love you.
- (SOFT CHUCKLE) I love you, too.

48
00:02:12,866 --> 00:02:13,866
(BOTH GRUNT)

49
00:02:18,438 --> 00:02:20,464
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

50
00:02:23,844 --> 00:02:25,676
(SIRENS WAILING)

51
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:29,180
MALE WAITER 1: <i>You don't
understand anything, okay?</i>

52
00:02:29,249 --> 00:02:32,515
<i>My friend just got blown up. Now,
I wanna know what happened?</i>

53
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,449
<i>Can you explain that to me?</i>

54
00:02:44,197 --> 00:02:46,564
We need to talk.

55
00:02:47,601 --> 00:02:48,864
Is everyone okay?

56
00:02:49,036 --> 00:02:51,870
A few first degree burns,
but that's it. They were lucky.

57
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,731
Any idea who might
have done this?

58
00:02:54,608 --> 00:02:57,407
I've made my share of enemies
over the years. Could be anyone.

59
00:02:57,611 --> 00:02:59,102
Why come after you now?

60
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:01,214
My oldest son is
getting married.

61
00:03:01,448 --> 00:03:04,782
When better to settle an old
score and hurt me and my family?

62
00:03:04,951 --> 00:03:06,214
Maybe.

63
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:08,617
Or maybe someone thinks
you're coming out of retirement?

64
00:03:09,256 --> 00:03:11,521
- I'm not.
- Good.

65
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:14,457
Doesn't mean I'm gonna stand
by after something like this.

66
00:03:15,962 --> 00:03:18,796
The Captain of Police was just
indicted for murder and sent to Arkham.

67
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:23,466
The last thing I need is you and your
men tearing up Gotham, looking for revenge.

68
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:26,336
I didn't start this.

69
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:31,171
I'll get to the bottom
of it. You have my word.

70
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,346
I'll give you one day.

71
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:48,662
COBBLEPOT: <i>As members of
the five families, you are well aware</i>

72
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:51,865
that with the tragic
downfall of Captain Barnes,

73
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:53,898
people are frightened.

74
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:58,797
They will be looking to
us for stability, to feel safe.

75
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,740
So,

76
00:04:01,341 --> 00:04:05,711
how does a 50% increase
on protection fees sound?

77
00:04:06,446 --> 00:04:08,486
- (LAUGHTER)
- BARBARA: <i>Sounds a little steep to me.</i>

78
00:04:08,949 --> 00:04:11,680
What do we have here?
A little family reunion?

79
00:04:11,852 --> 00:04:13,514
My invitation get
lost in the mail?

80
00:04:13,687 --> 00:04:18,057
No, this meeting is for grown-ups,
so I'm gonna have to ask you to leave.

81
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:19,225
Hmm.

82
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:20,587
Quick question.

83
00:04:21,027 --> 00:04:22,086
(GUNS COCKING)

84
00:04:22,395 --> 00:04:26,093
Is it, "How do I commit suicide?"
Because that answer is coming.

85
00:04:26,299 --> 00:04:28,768
Tabitha and Butch are
missing. Where are they?

86
00:04:29,636 --> 00:04:30,695
I have no idea.

87
00:04:31,304 --> 00:04:35,765
I have not seen Butch since his little
summer stock revival of the Red Hood Gang.

88
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,843
Let's cut the crap. Shall we?

89
00:04:38,011 --> 00:04:41,504
Tabitha has been helping Butch
hide since your little victory celebration.

90
00:04:41,681 --> 00:04:43,081
They're an item now, barf...

91
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,410
She's supposed to check in
every night, and she hasn't.

92
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:48,421
She's not answering her
phone, and no one has seen her.

93
00:04:48,755 --> 00:04:50,053
And you think I took them?

94
00:04:50,223 --> 00:04:51,247
Obviously.

95
00:04:51,424 --> 00:04:53,290
(MUFFLED LAUGHTER)

96
00:04:54,427 --> 00:04:57,022
How about this,
you lower your gun

97
00:04:57,297 --> 00:05:01,826
and beg my forgiveness
for this gross insubordination,

98
00:05:02,035 --> 00:05:04,436
and I might let you
walk out of here alive.

99
00:05:11,711 --> 00:05:13,009
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

100
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:19,012
My apologies.

101
00:05:19,419 --> 00:05:21,979
They must have run off
somewhere without telling me.

102
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:27,586
Love makes people do
crazy things, doesn't it?

103
00:05:30,564 --> 00:05:32,999
We have a history, you and I.

104
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:36,068
But if you ever point
a gun at me again,

105
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:39,467
Olga will be cleaning
your brains off the floor.

106
00:05:41,141 --> 00:05:43,372
She's a real wiz with stains.

107
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,044
Bye, Pengy.

108
00:05:49,816 --> 00:05:51,876
Everyone out, now!

109
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,986
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

110
00:05:57,691 --> 00:05:58,818
Are you checking up on me?

111
00:05:58,992 --> 00:06:00,927
What? No.

112
00:06:01,261 --> 00:06:03,890
Barbara Kean was just
here. She's looking for them.

113
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:07,862
- So?
- So, are you finished yet?

114
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:11,994
We've talked about this. I need
to work through my grief my way.

115
00:06:12,172 --> 00:06:14,732
COBBLEPOT: <i>Of
course, and I support you.</i>

116
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:18,675
Any chance you could work
through it a smidge faster?

117
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:21,547
<i>I am swamped today.</i>

118
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,377
(DIAL TONE)

119
00:06:26,186 --> 00:06:27,186
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

120
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:32,153
Sorry you had to hear that.
He can just be so self-centered.

121
00:06:33,493 --> 00:06:35,438
- What were we talking about?
- I'm gonna kill you!

122
00:06:35,462 --> 00:06:37,863
Oh! Right, how I
found you. (LAUGHING)

123
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:42,432
Well, it wasn't hard.

124
00:06:42,769 --> 00:06:44,203
The next time you
wanna disappear,

125
00:06:44,371 --> 00:06:46,382
<i>consider taking a sabbatical
from your favorite restaurant.</i>

126
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,638
Your love of Gusto's Eggplant
Parmesan isn't exactly a state secret.

127
00:06:49,809 --> 00:06:51,505
- (MUFFLED GROANS)
- Come here.

128
00:06:51,678 --> 00:06:55,308
That, with a healthy amount of
Midazolam in your food to knock you out.

129
00:06:55,515 --> 00:06:58,075
<i>A hundred bucks to your
delivery boy, who, by the way,</i>

130
00:06:58,318 --> 00:07:01,482
I get the feeling hasn't been
being tipped very well, Butch.

131
00:07:01,655 --> 00:07:03,146
(MUFFLED SPEECH)

132
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:06,190
I'm sorry. What was that?

133
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:09,852
(MUFFLED) You're gonna regret
this! You're gonna regret this.

134
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:13,692
If you touch one hair on
her head, I swear I'll kill you.

135
00:07:13,867 --> 00:07:16,359
Save your strength, big
guy. You're gonna need it.

136
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,303
And you tell Penguin
he's a coward.

137
00:07:19,539 --> 00:07:20,837
If he wants me dead,

138
00:07:21,007 --> 00:07:23,607
- he should come here and do it like a man.
- (DEVICE POWERING UP)

139
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:28,808
This has <i>nothing</i>
to do with Penguin.

140
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:32,980
And you are the coward.

141
00:07:33,353 --> 00:07:35,083
Killing an innocent woman.

142
00:07:35,322 --> 00:07:37,188
What? Who?

143
00:07:38,091 --> 00:07:39,525
Isabella.

144
00:07:39,693 --> 00:07:42,458
She was my everything,
and you took her from me!

145
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,792
What in the hell are
you talkin' about?

146
00:07:48,668 --> 00:07:51,228
I was hoping you'd be difficult.

147
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,235
- (ELECTRICITY ZAPPING)
- (GROANING)

148
00:07:54,874 --> 00:07:55,874
(LAUGHING)

149
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,280
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

150
00:08:04,551 --> 00:08:06,816
Hey. You okay?

151
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,554
Stomach.

152
00:08:08,722 --> 00:08:11,317
Being acting captain is
such a strain, why do it?

153
00:08:12,025 --> 00:08:13,550
I'm the senior guy around here.

154
00:08:13,727 --> 00:08:15,025
- What about Tuttle?
<i>- Tuttle?</i>

155
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:17,597
Guy shot a cat last week.

156
00:08:17,764 --> 00:08:20,029
- On purpose?
- Does it matter?

157
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,812
Look, I might not have always
seen eye-to-eye with Barnes,

158
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,270
but he was a good captain.

159
00:08:24,437 --> 00:08:26,338
Least I can do is
keep his seat warm

160
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,384
until they find some
kind of cure for this virus.

161
00:08:28,408 --> 00:08:31,242
Detective Gordon, car
bomb used a mercury switch

162
00:08:31,478 --> 00:08:32,810
with military grade plastic.

163
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:36,206
That's kind of high
end for a mob hit.

164
00:08:36,416 --> 00:08:37,577
That's not all.

165
00:08:37,751 --> 00:08:39,831
The explosive was laced
with some sort of accelerant.

166
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,956
<i>Made the explosion burn at 10
times the heat of standard C-4.</i>

167
00:08:43,289 --> 00:08:45,724
Whoever set this bomb
didn't want anything left behind.

168
00:08:45,925 --> 00:08:48,394
Only one guy I know
with that level of expertise.

169
00:08:48,561 --> 00:08:52,396
Ex-military nut job, goes
by the name of "Fuse."

170
00:08:54,401 --> 00:08:56,063
(SIRENS WAILING)

171
00:08:58,405 --> 00:08:59,429
This is our guy.

172
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,568
Not for nothing, ensuring Don Falcone's
safety is not why I wear the badge.

173
00:09:04,811 --> 00:09:07,645
- It's not just about him.
- You mean Lee?

174
00:09:07,814 --> 00:09:12,184
If you're worried, you could tell her not
to marry the son of a former crime boss.

175
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:19,089
GCPD!

176
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:29,593
<i>Dead, but still warm.</i>

177
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:32,131
Whoever did this
must've just left.

178
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:35,534
So, whoever hired Fuse to plant the
bomb doesn't want any loose ends?

179
00:09:36,276 --> 00:09:38,211
Looks like he was
on his way out of town.

180
00:09:38,511 --> 00:09:40,707
Must have figured his
employers weren't that forgiving.

181
00:09:41,648 --> 00:09:45,517
- Guy can pack, I'll give him that much.
- Once a soldier, always a soldier.

182
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:49,280
Bed sheets aren't tucked in.

183
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:59,930
Times, locations,
surveillance photos.

184
00:10:02,569 --> 00:10:05,198
- This doesn't make any sense.
- What?

185
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:08,435
Carmine's not the target.

186
00:10:09,642 --> 00:10:10,642
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

187
00:10:11,911 --> 00:10:14,380
(MOTORCYCLE REVVING)

188
00:10:18,718 --> 00:10:19,718
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

189
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:24,690
(TIRES SCREECH)

190
00:10:26,526 --> 00:10:27,526
(TIRES SCREECHING)

191
00:10:30,196 --> 00:10:31,664
- Down!
- (GUNSHOTS)

192
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:41,805
What the hell's going on?

193
00:10:42,242 --> 00:10:44,871
Carmine's not
the target. You are.

194
00:10:53,786 --> 00:10:55,186
<i>Et, euh, voilà.</i>

195
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,015
Thank you very
much, Master Bruce.

196
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:58,214
What is this?

197
00:10:58,424 --> 00:11:00,825
That is a Pennyworth
signature frittata.

198
00:11:02,395 --> 00:11:03,795
It's a crustless quiche.

199
00:11:04,931 --> 00:11:07,526
It's eggs, miss.
Just eat it, will you?

200
00:11:08,635 --> 00:11:10,365
Where's your mate, anyway?

201
00:11:10,537 --> 00:11:13,063
Conservatory.
Girl loves it there.

202
00:11:13,239 --> 00:11:17,370
Well, she's hardly what
you call "a girl," is she?

203
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:22,009
Yeah. Well, thanks for
the crustless egg thing.

204
00:11:22,215 --> 00:11:23,239
But I got errands to run.

205
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:25,336
<i>Uh, no, sorry, miss. No
one is to leave the house</i>

206
00:11:25,485 --> 00:11:27,545
until we find exactly
who is following you.

207
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,916
It's been days. I
can't take it anymore.

208
00:11:30,156 --> 00:11:32,091
I'm sorry. What is it
exactly that you object to?

209
00:11:32,258 --> 00:11:35,137
Is it the gourmet food, or the king-size
double-bed with the Egyptian linen?

210
00:11:35,161 --> 00:11:38,290
Would you tell the help here that I
can come and go as I please? Please?

211
00:11:38,464 --> 00:11:41,525
Alfred's right. It's not safe
for you to be in Gotham alone.

212
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:45,035
(SCOFFS) I've been in
Gotham alone my whole life.

213
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:48,364
I can take care of
myself. Nothing's changed.

214
00:11:48,841 --> 00:11:51,367
Yeah, you've made that clear.

215
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:55,148
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Nothing.

216
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,260
Those men were willing to kill
for this key, we need to know why.

217
00:11:58,284 --> 00:11:59,411
I'll be in the study.

218
00:11:59,586 --> 00:12:01,096
There's more books I
haven't gone through.

219
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,498
There has to be a reference
to the key somewhere.

220
00:12:02,522 --> 00:12:05,822
And have you stopped to consider
that maybe it's just an old key?

221
00:12:06,292 --> 00:12:07,453
No.

222
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:20,229
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACH)

223
00:12:22,508 --> 00:12:24,033
I'll get you some
breakfast, miss.

224
00:12:24,210 --> 00:12:28,375
You know, some of these plants
would do much better in direct sunlight.

225
00:12:28,548 --> 00:12:31,347
Could you turn off the alarm,
so I can put them outside?

226
00:12:31,517 --> 00:12:35,454
Well, maybe later. I'd rather not you be
walking around the grounds on your own.

227
00:12:38,191 --> 00:12:39,557
Can you smell this?

228
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,187
Beg your pardon?

229
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,762
Right here.

230
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:53,597
(EXHALES DEEPLY) What is that?

231
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:58,370
Just a mix of clove,
fenugreek, and yarrow root oils.

232
00:12:59,078 --> 00:13:00,137
It's lovely.

233
00:13:00,313 --> 00:13:02,282
- It is, isn't it?
- Yeah.

234
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,145
Now, I need you to tell
me something, okay?

235
00:13:06,319 --> 00:13:07,844
Anything.

236
00:13:08,488 --> 00:13:11,117
How do you turn off the alarm?

237
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,625
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

238
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:15,489
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

239
00:13:17,196 --> 00:13:18,494
This doesn't make any sense.

240
00:13:18,665 --> 00:13:20,657
Do you know anyone
who might want you dead?

241
00:13:21,701 --> 00:13:23,761
- You can't be serious.
- Everyone has enemies.

242
00:13:23,936 --> 00:13:25,370
No, Detective. They don't.

243
00:13:25,538 --> 00:13:27,530
Regardless, you need
to limit your exposure.

244
00:13:27,707 --> 00:13:30,142
Lay low for a while until I
can find out who's behind this.

245
00:13:30,343 --> 00:13:31,606
How do you propose I do that?

246
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:33,691
I'm picking up our
wedding rings this afternoon.

247
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,915
Lee and I are getting
married tomorrow.

248
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:38,650
Oh.

249
00:13:39,719 --> 00:13:41,079
You want me to
cancel the wedding.

250
00:13:41,187 --> 00:13:43,486
- I just wanna keep you safe.
- I'd bet you'd love that.

251
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:44,885
I run home to Lee.

252
00:13:45,058 --> 00:13:47,687
Tell her we need to hide until
Detective Gordon can save the day?

253
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:52,161
- This is not a time for ego.
- Are you talking to me about ego?

254
00:13:52,799 --> 00:13:55,132
How do I even know you're
gonna be able to find him?

255
00:13:55,301 --> 00:13:58,362
- Or that you'll even try?
- You need to trust me.

256
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:03,268
Whoever is behind this is gonna
keep coming until they get the job done.

257
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:08,874
If that's true, it doesn't matter
where we go, or what we do.

258
00:14:09,248 --> 00:14:12,275
As long as I got a target
on my back, Lee isn't safe.

259
00:14:19,592 --> 00:14:21,185
- Hey.
- Yeah.

260
00:14:21,661 --> 00:14:25,325
Keep an eye on Mario, don't let
him leave. What are you doing?

261
00:14:25,565 --> 00:14:28,034
- I'm keeping an eye on Mario.
- Don't look at him.

262
00:14:28,468 --> 00:14:29,468
What the hell's going on?

263
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:32,571
I don't know. Something doesn't
fit. I need to talk to Carmine.

264
00:14:32,739 --> 00:14:36,540
Maybe once he knows Mario's the
target, something will jog his memory.

265
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:38,177
Just keep it...

266
00:14:38,344 --> 00:14:40,506
I got it. I got it.

267
00:14:46,185 --> 00:14:47,414
(DOOR LOCK OPENS)

268
00:14:50,823 --> 00:14:51,950
Hello, Comrade.

269
00:14:53,025 --> 00:14:55,017
Comrade is not Russian word.

270
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:58,229
- Oh, shut up. Of course, it is.
- You shouldn't be here.

271
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,765
Relax. I know Penguin's
out for a few hours.

272
00:15:02,201 --> 00:15:03,533
I just wanna talk.

273
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:05,568
I don't know anything.

274
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:09,334
Listen. I grew up
in a place like this.

275
00:15:09,509 --> 00:15:13,503
A large staff of people
always coming and going.

276
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:18,184
Listening. You can't
help but overhear things.

277
00:15:19,986 --> 00:15:21,147
Is handsome ring.

278
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:24,119
(GASPS) It is.
And <i>very</i> expensive.

279
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:28,394
I bet it would look
just fabulous on you.

280
00:15:28,694 --> 00:15:30,219
(CHUCKLING)

281
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:31,930
(CLEARS THROAT)

282
00:15:33,199 --> 00:15:38,103
Mr. Penguin, he treat me
nice. I have warm feeling for him.

283
00:15:38,838 --> 00:15:40,101
But the other one...

284
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,366
Nygma?

285
00:15:42,074 --> 00:15:45,670
I don't know why
Mr. Penguin likes him so much.

286
00:15:46,179 --> 00:15:47,545
He could do better.

287
00:15:47,713 --> 00:15:50,808
Wait. You mean <i>likes, likes?</i>

288
00:15:52,351 --> 00:15:55,753
Wow. Okay, we should
definitely revisit that another time.

289
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:58,754
But what about Nygma? Did he
say anything about my missing friend?

290
00:15:58,925 --> 00:16:00,291
I don't know.

291
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:05,296
But I hear Mr. Nygma
talking about <i>special delivery.</i>

292
00:16:05,465 --> 00:16:09,926
But nothing come
to the house, but bill.

293
00:16:12,038 --> 00:16:13,768
"Stocks & Bondage?"

294
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:17,640
- (ELECTRICITY ZAPPING)
- (LAUGHING)

295
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:18,937
(GROANING)

296
00:16:20,746 --> 00:16:22,715
(MUFFLED GRUNTS)

297
00:16:23,683 --> 00:16:25,584
BUTCH: How many
times do I have to tell you?

298
00:16:26,352 --> 00:16:29,186
I have never even
heard of this woman.

299
00:16:29,722 --> 00:16:30,922
- (ELECTRICITY ZAPS)
- (GRUNTS)

300
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:35,185
Well, then I suppose I should
put my attention elsewhere.

301
00:16:35,361 --> 00:16:36,954
BUTCH: <i>No! No!</i>

302
00:16:37,363 --> 00:16:39,475
- Leave her out of this!
- ED: <i>Afraid I can't do that.</i>

303
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:42,731
She is an integral
part of your penance.

304
00:16:42,902 --> 00:16:44,613
<i>It was such a pleasant
surprise when I discovered</i>

305
00:16:44,637 --> 00:16:46,572
that the two of you were
together. (LAUGHING)

306
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:50,171
You know, after
the initial gag reflex.

307
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:55,809
You know, I bet this
girl doesn't even exist.

308
00:16:56,616 --> 00:17:00,053
I mean, come on, who would fall
in love with a freak show like you?

309
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:05,855
(CHUCKLING) Oh, wait, let me guess,
I bet she's got a certificate, too, huh?

310
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,065
- ED: <i>Mmm-hmm.</i>
- (LAUGHING)

311
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:08,473
- (ELECTRICITY ZAPS)
- (GROANING)

312
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:11,443
(MUFFLED) What do you want?

313
00:17:13,499 --> 00:17:15,400
Tell me what you want?

314
00:17:17,270 --> 00:17:18,670
Tell me what you want.

315
00:17:20,006 --> 00:17:23,465
I wanna break Butch's
heart before I end his life.

316
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:26,411
You know, kind of an
eye-for-an-eye thing.

317
00:17:26,579 --> 00:17:28,172
But in this case,

318
00:17:30,082 --> 00:17:31,880
I'll take a hand.

319
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,949
(DOOR OPENS)

320
00:17:37,290 --> 00:17:38,290
(INHALES DEEPLY)

321
00:17:38,457 --> 00:17:39,686
Is that vinegar?

322
00:17:40,493 --> 00:17:43,554
Vinegar and baking soda.
Takes tarnish off anything.

323
00:17:44,997 --> 00:17:46,829
Selina, that key is
hundreds of years old!

324
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,398
I'm not an idiot, you know?

325
00:17:49,936 --> 00:17:53,202
Maybe there's something
on the key that you can't see,

326
00:17:53,372 --> 00:17:55,637
because 100 years of
crap is covering it up?

327
00:17:58,511 --> 00:18:00,844
Why did you tell Ivy
we weren't a couple?

328
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:03,949
- Why did you tell her we were?
- Is that a trick question?

329
00:18:05,851 --> 00:18:08,218
Why can't we just be us?

330
00:18:10,656 --> 00:18:12,921
Can you take that key out
now? It's making me nervous.

331
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:14,116
(SOFT CHUCKLE)

332
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:18,630
SELINA: Mmm.

333
00:18:19,198 --> 00:18:21,258
There's an engraving on it.

334
00:18:23,302 --> 00:18:25,328
Like a bird, or something.

335
00:18:28,608 --> 00:18:32,204
Not just a bird. An owl.

336
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:35,773
- Uh... And?
- BRUCE: <i>Alfred!</i>

337
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:40,477
If you're right, merely possessing
this key could be seen as breaking

338
00:18:40,653 --> 00:18:43,533
your agreement with the people that
the woman in the owl mask represents.

339
00:18:43,656 --> 00:18:45,284
Which is why we
need to contact them.

340
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:47,836
They have to understand Ivy
didn't know what she was stealing.

341
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:49,294
Wait. Where is she anyhow?

342
00:18:53,733 --> 00:18:55,497
Oh, bloody hell. She's gone.

343
00:18:56,335 --> 00:18:57,535
How did she disable the alarm?

344
00:18:58,204 --> 00:18:59,581
Don't worry about
that now, all right?

345
00:18:59,605 --> 00:19:02,074
What's the big deal? She'll
be back when she's hungry.

346
00:19:02,241 --> 00:19:03,436
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

347
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,171
Wayne Manor.

348
00:19:09,348 --> 00:19:12,807
VOLK: <i>You have the
necklace, we have your friend.</i>

349
00:19:13,285 --> 00:19:15,311
We make exchange, no?

350
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:19,454
Where and when?

351
00:19:48,654 --> 00:19:50,179
We're supposed to
go down the manhole?

352
00:19:51,557 --> 00:19:55,324
That's what they said. All right,
give me the key. I'll sort it out.

353
00:19:56,095 --> 00:19:59,361
No. I need to speak
with them personally.

354
00:19:59,665 --> 00:20:01,566
Make sure they understand
this was a mistake.

355
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,302
Very well, Master Bruce.

356
00:20:08,607 --> 00:20:09,951
There's no way of
asking you to stay here

357
00:20:09,975 --> 00:20:11,944
that doesn't end with
you yelling at me, is there?

358
00:20:12,111 --> 00:20:13,340
No.

359
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:26,288
BRUCE: Over there.

360
00:20:26,592 --> 00:20:29,323
- SELINA: <i>Ivy?</i>
- It's about time.

361
00:20:38,037 --> 00:20:42,372
My name is Bruce Wayne. I
need to speak with Kathryn.

362
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:46,370
She needs to understand
I've honored our deal.

363
00:20:46,545 --> 00:20:50,482
Hand over the necklace, and you
get your friend back. That's the deal.

364
00:20:51,283 --> 00:20:52,911
You mean the key, don't you?

365
00:20:54,587 --> 00:20:57,250
You're not getting it back until I
talk to the people you work for.

366
00:20:58,057 --> 00:20:59,650
Maybe we just
kill you and take it?

367
00:20:59,825 --> 00:21:02,385
You think we're stupid
enough to bring it with us?

368
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:08,959
You really want it
back, I'd listen to him.

369
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:12,432
Put the tools
down. All right? Eh?

370
00:21:23,349 --> 00:21:26,376
I need reassurances my friends
are no longer in any danger.

371
00:21:27,853 --> 00:21:29,754
I need to speak to the
woman in the mask.

372
00:21:29,922 --> 00:21:33,825
Any assurances that
woman gives you are lies.

373
00:21:34,727 --> 00:21:35,990
How do you know?

374
00:21:36,162 --> 00:21:38,722
Because the people you are
talking about have no honor.

375
00:21:38,898 --> 00:21:42,630
And they will betray
you, as they betrayed us.

376
00:21:43,035 --> 00:21:45,334
Wait. You don't work for them?

377
00:21:45,738 --> 00:21:47,866
No. We work to destroy them.

378
00:21:51,210 --> 00:21:52,234
Who are they?

379
00:21:52,411 --> 00:21:56,007
They call themselves
"The Court of Owls."

380
00:21:59,084 --> 00:22:00,780
(SIRENS WAILING)

381
00:22:02,421 --> 00:22:05,050
- They're after Mario?
- Yes.

382
00:22:06,258 --> 00:22:10,161
- Where is he?
<i>- GCPD. He's safe. For now.</i>

383
00:22:10,429 --> 00:22:12,710
But I can't help him if you
don't tell me what's going on.

384
00:22:13,532 --> 00:22:15,194
You think I'm holding
something back?

385
00:22:15,568 --> 00:22:18,561
Military grade
explosion? The clean-up?

386
00:22:18,804 --> 00:22:21,865
<i>A sword-wielding
assassin in broad daylight.</i>

387
00:22:22,074 --> 00:22:23,736
This doesn't feel
like a mob grudge.

388
00:22:24,710 --> 00:22:25,905
What else is there?

389
00:22:27,279 --> 00:22:29,339
Could Mario be
mixed up in something?

390
00:22:30,549 --> 00:22:34,077
- Is that what you came to ask me?
- I'm working the evidence I have.

391
00:22:35,154 --> 00:22:36,782
I understand why
you'd want to believe

392
00:22:36,956 --> 00:22:39,755
the man who's marrying Lee
must be mixed up in something.

393
00:22:40,559 --> 00:22:44,496
My son is the most decent
person I've ever known.

394
00:22:45,731 --> 00:22:47,165
He's not like us.

395
00:22:47,333 --> 00:22:48,333
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

396
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:52,137
That just tells me there's
something you don't know.

397
00:22:54,473 --> 00:22:56,066
BULLOCK: <i>Jim, Mario's gone.</i>

398
00:22:56,242 --> 00:22:57,682
You were supposed
to keep him there.

399
00:22:57,743 --> 00:22:58,743
I know, I tried,

400
00:22:58,911 --> 00:23:01,574
but he said he didn't trust you
or the GCPD to take care of this.

401
00:23:01,747 --> 00:23:04,478
So, he was going to.
Whatever the hell that means.

402
00:23:06,018 --> 00:23:07,018
What is it?

403
00:23:07,186 --> 00:23:09,587
Mario just walked
out of the GCPD.

404
00:23:09,788 --> 00:23:12,223
Think he's gonna try
to finish this himself.

405
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:13,391
How?

406
00:23:13,726 --> 00:23:15,160
I have a pretty good idea.

407
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:23,428
- Can I help you?
- BARBARA: I hope so.

408
00:23:23,903 --> 00:23:26,566
I had something that was
supposed to be delivered to me?

409
00:23:26,739 --> 00:23:28,002
Could you check your records?

410
00:23:28,274 --> 00:23:30,903
Sure. Let me check the safe.
Uh, what was the last name?

411
00:23:31,110 --> 00:23:32,237
"Nygma."

412
00:23:32,811 --> 00:23:34,643
Oh. That item was
already delivered.

413
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:36,540
Great.

414
00:23:36,949 --> 00:23:39,885
Well, I guess as long
as I'm already here

415
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:43,283
I should pick up something
for the weekend. Right?

416
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,257
(SOFTLY) Mmm.

417
00:23:47,159 --> 00:23:48,957
Well, this looks fun.

418
00:23:49,561 --> 00:23:51,530
Could I ask a favor of you?

419
00:23:51,830 --> 00:23:53,196
- Uh, Todd.
<i>- Todd.</i>

420
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:55,591
Could you show
me how this works?

421
00:23:56,335 --> 00:23:57,335
(SIGHS)

422
00:23:57,770 --> 00:23:59,610
We're not really supposed
to... (CLEARS THROAT)

423
00:23:59,905 --> 00:24:02,101
I won't tell if you don't.

424
00:24:04,143 --> 00:24:06,078
It's pretty basic, really.

425
00:24:06,312 --> 00:24:09,043
Um, you just put your
arms through here,

426
00:24:09,214 --> 00:24:12,150
and then your head through
here, and then you bring it up.

427
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:13,980
And then... Oh!

428
00:24:14,687 --> 00:24:16,485
Do you like role play, Todd?

429
00:24:17,990 --> 00:24:18,990
Good.

430
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:23,289
I will play the beautiful,
coquettish bank robber

431
00:24:23,529 --> 00:24:25,498
who needs to get into that safe,

432
00:24:25,764 --> 00:24:29,360
and you get to play the
lucky, young shopkeeper

433
00:24:29,668 --> 00:24:31,796
who gives her the
combination, okay?

434
00:24:33,572 --> 00:24:36,064
My friend was taken
by this man, Nygma.

435
00:24:36,875 --> 00:24:39,208
I need to know where she is.

436
00:24:39,745 --> 00:24:43,807
If I find her, I could come back
here and personally thank you.

437
00:24:43,983 --> 00:24:45,315
(WHIMPERING)

438
00:24:46,185 --> 00:24:50,179
Give Mommy the combination.

439
00:24:53,359 --> 00:24:55,919
(STAMMERING) Nine, 25, 72.

440
00:24:56,195 --> 00:24:57,527
Good.

441
00:24:58,197 --> 00:24:59,197
(SIGHS)

442
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:10,903
Nygma, you sick bastard.

443
00:25:11,276 --> 00:25:15,077
(STAMMERING) Hey?
You can't just leave me here!

444
00:25:15,647 --> 00:25:16,647
<i>Hello?</i>

445
00:25:25,691 --> 00:25:29,389
(GASPS) Oh, goodie!
You're finally awake.

446
00:25:29,561 --> 00:25:30,961
The show continues.

447
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:32,721
(MIMICKING DRUMROLL)

448
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:35,233
Ta-da!

449
00:25:37,403 --> 00:25:38,769
I designed it myself.

450
00:25:39,671 --> 00:25:42,072
<i>You wanna see
how it works? Okay!</i>

451
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:43,942
I love a captive audience.

452
00:25:44,343 --> 00:25:48,678
So, we'll set the timer
for, say, 55 seconds.

453
00:25:48,947 --> 00:25:53,078
Now, when the timer hits zero,
the spring-loaded blade is released.

454
00:25:53,752 --> 00:25:57,519
- (TIMER TICKING)
- Simple. Now, for the fun part.

455
00:25:57,689 --> 00:26:01,683
You can stop the blade from being
released, if you click this little button.

456
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:02,860
But if you do,

457
00:26:03,028 --> 00:26:08,228
it will send a fatal jolt of
electricity to zap Butch.

458
00:26:09,601 --> 00:26:10,796
It's a simple test, really.

459
00:26:11,703 --> 00:26:16,368
Stop the blade from
falling and kill Butch, or...

460
00:26:16,542 --> 00:26:17,542
(TIMER DINGS)

461
00:26:22,581 --> 00:26:23,581
Mmm!

462
00:26:25,451 --> 00:26:26,783
The choice...

463
00:26:28,487 --> 00:26:29,487
(GRUNTS)

464
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:32,756
my dear, is yours.

465
00:26:32,958 --> 00:26:35,951
Will we hear the
zap of heartbreak,

466
00:26:36,829 --> 00:26:39,697
or the sound of
one-hand clapping.

467
00:26:39,865 --> 00:26:41,857
(LAUGHING)

468
00:26:45,971 --> 00:26:47,667
(METAL CHAINS CLINKING)

469
00:26:48,006 --> 00:26:49,531
My name is Volk.

470
00:26:49,708 --> 00:26:50,708
(CUFFS CLICK)

471
00:26:51,043 --> 00:26:54,070
My brother, Jacob,
and that's Dmitry.

472
00:26:55,247 --> 00:26:56,738
What's with the stupid mask?

473
00:26:58,383 --> 00:27:01,842
I like you. You remind
me of my sister in Kiev.

474
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:04,552
Dmitry is an initiate.

475
00:27:04,823 --> 00:27:08,021
<i>The mask ensures his
silence until he proves himself</i>

476
00:27:08,327 --> 00:27:09,590
and becomes a full member.

477
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:11,661
Of what? Who are you?

478
00:27:12,698 --> 00:27:16,999
We are called "the Whisper Gang."
Gotham's most notorious smugglers.

479
00:27:17,870 --> 00:27:21,034
We used to number in the hundreds
until the Court saw our growing strength

480
00:27:21,206 --> 00:27:24,108
and they offered
us a partnership,

481
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:25,641
only to betray us.

482
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:28,908
Many escaped back to Ukraine,
but a few of us stayed back,

483
00:27:29,081 --> 00:27:31,880
hoping to find a way
to enact revenge.

484
00:27:32,985 --> 00:27:35,454
- And we did.
- The key?

485
00:27:36,989 --> 00:27:38,457
But what does it open?

486
00:27:39,591 --> 00:27:40,615
A safe.

487
00:27:42,628 --> 00:27:46,793
It is in one of the
Court's buildings, here.

488
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:52,538
Inside, there is a device that
we believe can destroy them.

489
00:27:52,971 --> 00:27:54,906
What? Like some kind of weapon?

490
00:27:55,574 --> 00:27:57,839
Oh, honestly, we don't know.

491
00:27:58,010 --> 00:27:59,103
We captured a member.

492
00:27:59,278 --> 00:28:01,338
But even he didn't know
what's inside the safe.

493
00:28:01,547 --> 00:28:05,814
Only that the Court fears it falling
into the hands of their enemies.

494
00:28:05,984 --> 00:28:08,385
Wait, wouldn't they
know you stole it?

495
00:28:08,554 --> 00:28:10,514
They're probably waiting
for you to show up there.

496
00:28:10,656 --> 00:28:13,524
No. Because, originally,
the safe had two keys.

497
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:17,227
The Court still has one of them.
And the second one was thought lost.

498
00:28:17,563 --> 00:28:19,361
Until we found it.

499
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:22,429
You mean, <i>we</i> did?

500
00:28:24,002 --> 00:28:26,233
The Court of Owls
killed my parents.

501
00:28:26,471 --> 00:28:29,600
I stood down because I thought
there was no way to defeat them.

502
00:28:30,842 --> 00:28:32,105
What are you proposing?

503
00:28:32,811 --> 00:28:37,078
If what you're saying is true,
and there is something in that safe,

504
00:28:38,450 --> 00:28:40,612
then that's no longer the case.

505
00:28:42,888 --> 00:28:44,447
(DOOR OPENS)

506
00:28:45,457 --> 00:28:47,551
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

507
00:28:51,496 --> 00:28:52,496
JIM: Mario?

508
00:28:55,534 --> 00:28:58,971
You really think this is a good
idea? Using yourself as bait?

509
00:28:59,137 --> 00:29:00,969
If those guys are out
there, Lee isn't safe.

510
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,833
They're pros. You're
gonna get killed.

511
00:29:03,008 --> 00:29:04,374
What do you care?

512
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:06,972
- Why would someone wanna kill you?
- I have no idea.

513
00:29:07,145 --> 00:29:08,238
Because it seems to me

514
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:10,848
an operation like this
doesn't happen for no reason.

515
00:29:11,383 --> 00:29:12,860
And putting yourself
in the cross hairs

516
00:29:12,884 --> 00:29:14,644
feels a lot like someone
protecting a secret.

517
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:18,452
I wanna protect Lee. That's it.

518
00:29:21,693 --> 00:29:24,720
We're sitting ducks in here. We
need to get away from bystanders.

519
00:29:26,531 --> 00:29:28,193
- They're here.
- What?

520
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:29,433
Get down!

521
00:29:29,601 --> 00:29:30,601
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

522
00:29:35,540 --> 00:29:36,540
WOMAN: No! No!

523
00:29:37,709 --> 00:29:38,709
(GROANS)

524
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:43,876
(MEN GRUNTING)

525
00:29:46,285 --> 00:29:47,719
(MARIO STRAINING)

526
00:29:49,655 --> 00:29:50,655
(SCREAMING)

527
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:55,188
You could have killed
her! Who sent you?

528
00:29:55,394 --> 00:29:57,727
Why are you coming after me?

529
00:29:58,397 --> 00:30:01,663
(CHOKING) You know why.

530
00:30:06,571 --> 00:30:07,571
(GRUNTS)

531
00:30:07,739 --> 00:30:10,903
- (SIRENS WAILING)
- (HANDCUFFS CLICKING)

532
00:30:17,649 --> 00:30:19,242
(BUTCH AND TABITHA GRUNTING)

533
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:22,317
Hey, Ed, come on. Come
on, let's talk about this, huh?

534
00:30:22,521 --> 00:30:24,752
Come on, Ed. You
don't have to do this.

535
00:30:25,257 --> 00:30:27,726
Come on, let's talk about
this. Come on! Listen!

536
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:30,963
I told you, I've never heard
of anyone named Isabelle.

537
00:30:31,430 --> 00:30:34,559
Isabella! Why is
that so difficult?

538
00:30:34,866 --> 00:30:36,994
<i>Also, I'm not the one you
should be pleading with.</i>

539
00:30:37,169 --> 00:30:40,606
Your life is in her <i>hand.</i>

540
00:30:43,041 --> 00:30:44,236
What difference does it make?

541
00:30:44,476 --> 00:30:47,810
You're gonna kill me one
way, or the other, right?

542
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:49,578
Good point. (CHUCKLES)

543
00:30:50,716 --> 00:30:52,480
New deal.

544
00:30:52,784 --> 00:30:56,346
If she loves you enough to
sacrifice her hand. Twinsies.

545
00:30:56,655 --> 00:30:58,089
In exchange for your life.

546
00:30:58,256 --> 00:31:01,784
I swear on the memory
of my beloved Isabella,

547
00:31:01,993 --> 00:31:03,859
I will set you both free.

548
00:31:04,429 --> 00:31:05,429
(CLICKING)

549
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:08,193
(TIMER TICKING)

550
00:31:12,637 --> 00:31:15,334
Tabby, baby, you don't wanna...

551
00:31:20,011 --> 00:31:23,311
- We can get out of here. We can...
- I like you, Butch. I really do.

552
00:31:24,616 --> 00:31:28,018
But to be completely honest, I'm
not exactly in a love place right now.

553
00:31:28,186 --> 00:31:29,186
(LAUGHS)

554
00:31:32,791 --> 00:31:34,282
Sorry, big fella.

555
00:31:34,493 --> 00:31:38,294
I wish I could say that I was surprised,
but I knew that she was going to say that.

556
00:31:38,497 --> 00:31:40,159
(WHISPERS) It's
why I made the offer.

557
00:31:40,832 --> 00:31:43,495
Any final words? I
would keep it brief.

558
00:31:47,005 --> 00:31:49,600
BUTCH: <i>Tabby, baby,</i>

559
00:31:50,442 --> 00:31:53,879
the last few weeks have
been the best of my life.

560
00:31:55,447 --> 00:31:57,416
And it's okay you don't love me.

561
00:31:58,717 --> 00:32:01,186
'Cause I love you.

562
00:32:02,020 --> 00:32:05,286
And for a guy like
me, that's enough.

563
00:32:06,057 --> 00:32:08,754
And, you, you're
damn right I killed her.

564
00:32:09,461 --> 00:32:11,396
I killed the woman you loved.

565
00:32:11,563 --> 00:32:15,330
You know what she said to me
right before I put a bullet in her brain?

566
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:17,368
<i>You know what she told me?</i>

567
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:20,162
She said she wished she
would've been with a real man.

568
00:32:20,439 --> 00:32:21,439
Hey, Butch?

569
00:32:23,041 --> 00:32:24,041
Yeah?

570
00:32:25,644 --> 00:32:26,737
You're sweet.

571
00:32:30,582 --> 00:32:32,847
No! No!

572
00:32:33,018 --> 00:32:34,018
(GASPS)

573
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:43,322
Untie me!

574
00:32:43,495 --> 00:32:46,488
Please untie me! She's
gotta get to a hospital! Quick!

575
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:49,601
You said that you put
a bullet in her head.

576
00:32:49,768 --> 00:32:53,000
Isabella died in a car crash.
The break lines were cut.

577
00:32:53,171 --> 00:32:55,572
I don't care! I told you
I never heard of her.

578
00:32:55,774 --> 00:32:57,902
You really didn't kill her?

579
00:32:58,076 --> 00:33:01,604
No! Untie me! She's gotta
get to a hospital! Come on!

580
00:33:03,882 --> 00:33:04,882
(GUN COCKS)

581
00:33:07,586 --> 00:33:09,919
I'd put that hand on some ice.

582
00:33:15,026 --> 00:33:16,026
(HORNS BLARING)

583
00:33:19,064 --> 00:33:20,794
Neither of you recognize him?

584
00:33:21,600 --> 00:33:22,624
No.

585
00:33:24,135 --> 00:33:25,398
Has he said anything?

586
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,328
Not a peep.

587
00:33:27,606 --> 00:33:30,075
Hey. I ran your guy's prints.

588
00:33:30,242 --> 00:33:32,768
They're not in the system.
Which, considering he's a pro,

589
00:33:32,978 --> 00:33:34,207
wasn't that hard to believe.

590
00:33:34,379 --> 00:33:36,712
I know. Still. Now, that we
have him, we should work him.

591
00:33:36,882 --> 00:33:38,111
Find out who's behind this.

592
00:33:38,283 --> 00:33:39,945
You better act
quick. Call came in.

593
00:33:40,118 --> 00:33:42,519
They're transferring him
to a Federal facility upstate.

594
00:33:42,721 --> 00:33:44,553
What! No, no, no. We
can't let this guy leave!

595
00:33:44,723 --> 00:33:48,421
What can I do? My hands were
tied. The Feds want him, they get him.

596
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:49,784
Question is why.

597
00:33:49,961 --> 00:33:52,658
Maybe somebody wants
him out of this precinct.

598
00:33:53,431 --> 00:33:54,865
Away from us.

599
00:33:55,100 --> 00:33:57,968
I don't know anyone with
that kind of pull. Do you?

600
00:34:04,009 --> 00:34:05,375
JIM: <i>The other assassin.</i>

601
00:34:06,611 --> 00:34:08,512
You wanna tell me what
happened in the store?

602
00:34:08,747 --> 00:34:12,775
There's nothing to tell. He came
after me, I did what I needed to do.

603
00:34:17,589 --> 00:34:18,887
You called her?

604
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:23,658
She deserves to know what's
going on. Either you tell her, or I will.

605
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:43,414
(DOOR CLOSES)

606
00:34:45,050 --> 00:34:46,780
FALCONE: <i>I think I
know who sent you,</i>

607
00:34:47,953 --> 00:34:49,945
but I need to know for sure.

608
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:54,415
And we both know that
you're not going to tell me.

609
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:57,788
So...

610
00:35:03,735 --> 00:35:05,863
So, how does it feel?

611
00:35:06,471 --> 00:35:08,963
BULLOCK: I don't know.
Maybe I could be Captain?

612
00:35:09,174 --> 00:35:11,006
Yell at people for
not having proof,

613
00:35:11,176 --> 00:35:13,168
or at one of my detectives

614
00:35:13,345 --> 00:35:16,372
for going after a pair of
assassins all by his lonesome!

615
00:35:16,982 --> 00:35:18,541
- Not bad.
- Right?

616
00:35:18,717 --> 00:35:21,118
Very interesting
play, by the way.

617
00:35:21,286 --> 00:35:22,846
It's not every day
that you get to save

618
00:35:22,921 --> 00:35:24,890
the man who's marrying
the woman you love.

619
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:28,025
Yeah. I'm really something.

620
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,352
It's not too late, Jim.

621
00:35:31,997 --> 00:35:33,989
Lee deserves to
know how you feel.

622
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:37,603
God knows I know that
life gives us enough regret.

623
00:35:37,769 --> 00:35:39,897
There's no need adding to it.

624
00:35:42,607 --> 00:35:44,235
- Oh, crap.
- I know it's hard.

625
00:35:44,409 --> 00:35:45,886
It's just, it's something
you have to...

626
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:46,910
Falcone!

627
00:35:48,013 --> 00:35:49,345
(ASSASSIN SCREAMING)

628
00:35:49,547 --> 00:35:51,379
(CONTINUES SCREAMING)

629
00:35:52,851 --> 00:35:53,851
(COUGHING)

630
00:35:54,119 --> 00:35:55,212
(BLOOD SPUTTERING)

631
00:35:55,387 --> 00:35:56,387
(ASSASSIN SPITS)

632
00:35:57,489 --> 00:35:58,489
(DOOR OPENS)

633
00:35:58,757 --> 00:36:00,623
Falcone, up against the wall.

634
00:36:00,792 --> 00:36:03,318
- What're you doing?
- Just having a chat.

635
00:36:04,663 --> 00:36:08,100
Turns out our friend here works
for a former associate of mine.

636
00:36:08,266 --> 00:36:11,794
So, now that I know who's
behind this, I can take care of it.

637
00:36:12,037 --> 00:36:13,733
My way. It's over.

638
00:36:13,905 --> 00:36:15,149
You think you're
gonna walk away?

639
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:17,404
You just assaulted a
suspect in police custody.

640
00:36:19,477 --> 00:36:21,503
He won't be pressing charges.

641
00:36:22,313 --> 00:36:25,112
I'm gonna find out what happened
today. Who's pulling the strings.

642
00:36:25,283 --> 00:36:27,411
And how Mario's
involved. Trust me.

643
00:36:28,386 --> 00:36:30,582
If I were you, I'd let it go.

644
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,590
VOLK: Gather the men.

645
00:36:40,832 --> 00:36:42,630
Tell them we're joining
forces with the boy.

646
00:36:42,801 --> 00:36:44,178
I will brief them
tomorrow night myself.

647
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:45,226
TALON: <i>Volk!</i>

648
00:36:46,404 --> 00:36:48,270
Dmitry, eyes!

649
00:36:51,910 --> 00:36:52,910
(CHOKES)

650
00:37:06,691 --> 00:37:08,683
<i>We know you've been
searching for the second key.</i>

651
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:11,856
Have you found it?

652
00:37:12,464 --> 00:37:15,298
(BOTH GRUNTING)

653
00:37:23,208 --> 00:37:24,699
I'll ask you again.

654
00:37:24,976 --> 00:37:28,037
Have you found the second key?

655
00:37:28,947 --> 00:37:30,916
(GROWLING) Why don't
you ask Dmitry? Huh?

656
00:37:31,516 --> 00:37:33,917
(BOTH GRUNTING)

657
00:37:35,453 --> 00:37:36,546
(SCREAMS AND GROANS)

658
00:37:41,893 --> 00:37:43,225
(BLOOD DRIPPING)

659
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:49,798
(SIRENS WAILING)

660
00:37:50,001 --> 00:37:52,732
You think she'll be okay? Think
they can reattach the hand?

661
00:37:52,904 --> 00:37:55,169
Please. She's tough
as nails. She'll be fine.

662
00:37:55,340 --> 00:37:56,717
BUTCH: You know
this is war, right?

663
00:37:56,741 --> 00:37:59,404
Nygma, Penguin, anyone who
stands with them, they're all dead.

664
00:37:59,577 --> 00:38:03,105
This woman, Isabella. Nygma
said she was a librarian, right?

665
00:38:03,281 --> 00:38:05,580
Well, who kills a librarian?
I mean, what's the motive?

666
00:38:05,784 --> 00:38:06,784
I don't know.

667
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:10,285
Maybe someone had an overdue
book and things got out of hand.

668
00:38:10,622 --> 00:38:12,750
Excuse me, but
you just can't walk...

669
00:38:13,658 --> 00:38:15,149
Come on! Come on! I got it.

670
00:38:15,326 --> 00:38:16,988
NURSE: We got a
hand here, people! Hand!

671
00:38:17,162 --> 00:38:21,122
You cut someone's break lines, you
know where they're going and when.

672
00:38:21,432 --> 00:38:23,094
You know...

673
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:25,095
You know them.

674
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:26,303
(LAUGHS)

675
00:38:26,638 --> 00:38:28,038
I know who did it.

676
00:38:28,439 --> 00:38:30,635
I know who killed the librarian.

677
00:38:31,242 --> 00:38:32,242
Who?

678
00:38:32,410 --> 00:38:33,854
The same person
who's in love with Nygma,

679
00:38:33,878 --> 00:38:35,574
and doesn't wanna
share him. (GIGGLING)

680
00:38:35,847 --> 00:38:38,009
Okay. One woman in love
with that psychotic bean pole

681
00:38:38,183 --> 00:38:39,481
defies explanation, but two?

682
00:38:39,651 --> 00:38:41,119
Who said anything about a woman?

683
00:38:41,286 --> 00:38:42,286
(BARBARA CHUCKLES)

684
00:38:42,954 --> 00:38:46,015
I am tired of sitting
at the kids table.

685
00:38:46,224 --> 00:38:49,820
If I'm right, we can have
way more than vengeance.

686
00:38:50,428 --> 00:38:51,987
<i>We can have it all.</i>

687
00:38:52,697 --> 00:38:56,862
We don't need to go to war.
All we need to do is start one.

688
00:38:58,469 --> 00:38:59,767
(BARBARA GIGGLING)

689
00:39:06,444 --> 00:39:08,504
There must've been some mistake.

690
00:39:08,913 --> 00:39:10,609
We don't make mistakes.

691
00:39:10,815 --> 00:39:13,410
I've always done whatever
the Court has asked of me.

692
00:39:14,118 --> 00:39:15,814
<i>Even against my own interest.</i>

693
00:39:16,187 --> 00:39:19,180
I got you Indian Hill when
Maroni refused to sell.

694
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:21,690
No one is questioning
your loyalty.

695
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:25,194
If this isn't about me, then
why are you trying to kill my son?

696
00:39:26,264 --> 00:39:27,823
There are things
you're not privy to.

697
00:39:27,999 --> 00:39:29,991
That's not an answer!

698
00:39:30,501 --> 00:39:33,130
It will have to do.

699
00:39:34,505 --> 00:39:37,339
We both know the level
of disruption I can cause.

700
00:39:38,076 --> 00:39:39,977
You think we're scared of you?

701
00:39:40,144 --> 00:39:42,909
The car bomb was designed
to look like a mob hit.

702
00:39:43,281 --> 00:39:46,615
You didn't want me to
find out it was you. I have.

703
00:39:47,085 --> 00:39:48,917
<i>I don't care about your reasons.</i>

704
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:50,720
If my son is harmed in any way,

705
00:39:50,889 --> 00:39:53,484
I will come after you
with everything I have.

706
00:39:53,791 --> 00:39:55,453
You won't win.

707
00:39:56,327 --> 00:39:59,991
If my son is dead,
winning won't be the point.

708
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:04,297
Gotham will burn.

709
00:40:05,036 --> 00:40:08,131
This city is on
the brink of chaos.

710
00:40:08,673 --> 00:40:11,108
<i>Only we can save it.</i>

711
00:40:11,643 --> 00:40:14,169
We will expect your
assistance when called on.

712
00:40:14,445 --> 00:40:17,074
Until then, your son is safe.

713
00:40:17,715 --> 00:40:19,707
At least from us.

714
00:40:20,718 --> 00:40:22,710
What aren't you telling me?

715
00:40:23,855 --> 00:40:26,120
A great many things.

716
00:40:28,226 --> 00:40:30,286
Enjoy your dinner.

717
00:40:46,544 --> 00:40:47,910
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

718
00:40:50,381 --> 00:40:51,713
(KNOCKING CONTINUES)

719
00:40:59,991 --> 00:41:01,015
Hey.

720
00:41:07,332 --> 00:41:09,358
Is everything okay?

721
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:13,066
I was on my way to
the rehearsal dinner,

722
00:41:13,338 --> 00:41:15,739
then I heard myself telling
the cab driver your address.

723
00:41:17,275 --> 00:41:20,074
Mario told me
everything about today.

724
00:41:20,244 --> 00:41:21,964
How you risked your
own life to make sure...

725
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:24,072
I didn't do it for him.

726
00:41:25,416 --> 00:41:26,416
I know.

727
00:41:28,052 --> 00:41:29,418
He's a good man.

728
00:41:29,687 --> 00:41:30,687
Uh-huh.

729
00:41:34,459 --> 00:41:35,722
Tell me.

730
00:41:36,761 --> 00:41:37,761
What?

731
00:41:38,529 --> 00:41:40,725
What you have to tell me.

732
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:47,961
I missed my chance to
give you the life you deserve.

733
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:51,643
<i>To make you happy.</i>

734
00:41:52,443 --> 00:41:55,811
But I do want that for you.

735
00:41:56,047 --> 00:41:57,811
More than anything.

736
00:42:01,152 --> 00:42:04,247
Why does it feel like we
keep saying goodbye?

737
00:42:06,491 --> 00:42:09,154
Maybe it's all we have left.

738
00:42:09,460 --> 00:42:12,396
Or we just haven't
done it properly yet.

739
00:42:21,439 --> 00:42:23,203
Goodbye, James Gordon.

740
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:26,543
(DOOR OPENS)

741
00:42:42,527 --> 00:42:46,055
MAN: Yo, Peeping Tom! You lost?

742
00:42:46,998 --> 00:42:49,490
Lucky for you,
we sell directions!

743
00:42:51,502 --> 00:42:54,631
Price, everything you've got.

744
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,366
MARIO: <i>She loves him.</i>

745
00:42:56,541 --> 00:42:57,907
<i>She loves him. She loves him.</i>

746
00:42:58,076 --> 00:42:59,076
You deaf?

747
00:42:59,277 --> 00:43:00,277
MARIO: <i>She loves him.</i>

748
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:02,137
- I said...
- MARIO: <i>She loves him.</i>

749
00:43:02,680 --> 00:43:04,148
Hey, man! What...

750
00:43:04,382 --> 00:43:05,382
(MAN GROANING)

751
00:43:06,784 --> 00:43:11,313
- (CHOKING)
- She loves me! And I won't let her go!

752
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:16,258
She loves <i>me!</i>

753
00:43:26,137 --> 00:43:28,163
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

754
00:44:01,205 --> 00:44:02,205
English -SDH
